# Bandit configuration. It holds one exclude of one named file and nothing else: no skips line (that would hide a rule in the whole tree), no tests
# line, no second exclude. The path is the plain path without a leading dot and slash. bandit stops with exit 2 when the tree holds a second .bandit file,
# so this is the only one.
[bandit]
# B404, B603, B607: scripts/lib/agentd_build.py is a build-time helper (the worker image build, deploy and the fake-engine test step), not product
# runtime logic. It runs cargo, zig and git through argument lists, never a shell.
exclude = scripts/lib/agentd_build.py
